(5784870, 840767, 43594, '<td valign="top">Few people asked what do I mean by ''squashed oil'' and, as i''m not an English native speaker, here are a few more details: by squashed oil I mean, basically, that all 3 ''ingredients'' - oil, ink and water - should be quite strongly shaken/mixed/agitated with a stick or something else. By doing this you get lots of small bubbles which immediately start ''moving'' and then getting back together and so on... <br/>Hope this is quite clear. :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2009-12-29 04:37:09.</i></td>', 'Few people asked what do I mean by ''squashed oil'' and, as i''m not an English native speaker, here are a few more details: by squashed oil I mean, basically, that all 3 ''ingredients'' - oil, ink and water - should be quite strongly shaken/mixed/agitated with a stick or something else. By doing this you get lots of small bubbles which immediately start ''moving'' and then getting back together and so on... Hope this is quite clear. :)', '2009-12-29 02:20:32.000000', '2009-12-29 04:37:09.000000', 0),
